          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-21-diagnosing-cryptococcal-disease.md",
      "source_hash": "e5941fef2ab4ff142d5ef252e9590f38e8673554034cb08f4a2318ad0a699dc7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that WHO's 2018 recommendations on diagnosing cryptococcal disease remain unchanged.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-211-background.md",
      "source_hash": "0c7b5f2a5bb5a139c65dddd3f2fff38224cb8b657777334e6df2d2e0afb11991",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Stresses early diagnosis of cryptococcal meningitis and sets out the 2018 recommendation for prompt lumbar puncture with opening pressure measurement and rapid antigen testing. It describes diagnostic approaches according to access to lumbar puncture and rapid tests and lists contraindications to lumbar puncture.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-2-recommendations-on-diagnosing-and-preventing-c.md",
      "source_hash": "0cb4824fcf0e5d76f6d20ea66d505b3a3110cb21e380a0eaccb41d8cc571ed1b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A summary chart of the diagnostic approach to cryptococcal meningitis, depending on whether lumbar puncture and rapid antigen tests are available.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-212-rationale-for-the-recommendations.md",
      "source_hash": "868f4db00bc7bc8da8ac4f1c7500632b7d4cdaf8a6a78751fdb89e7dd6a1b396",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that rapid cryptococcal antigen assays are preferred over India ink because they are more accurate and need less skill, and why lateral-flow assays are favoured. It notes that blood antigen testing does not replace lumbar puncture where feasible and that the adult recommendations are extended to children.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-22-preventing-and-screening-for-cryptococcal-dis.md",
      "source_hash": "adc66a62c215a84f3c12c65487a352db92bf2c84c24bcb8fa7f6cddd21f8ba2e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that WHO's 2018 recommendations on preventing and screening for cryptococcal disease remain unchanged.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-221-background.md",
      "source_hash": "a1905e079efac1e8f2b3421e1fa45bce9922d37d2fd629b2cc5ce3d12105a2e4",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that early ART is the main way to prevent cryptococcal disease and sets out the 2018 recommendations on antigen screening before ART, pre-emptive antifungal therapy and fluconazole prophylaxis where screening is unavailable. It stresses evaluating everyone who screens positive for meningitis.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-012",
      "source": "sections/sec-012-222-rationale-for-the-recommendations.md",
      "source_hash": "14de42f3e14d559612098ddf67dc7419c3dd01c65d76d1961fb316a407339547",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Gives the rationale for screening adults and adolescents with low CD4 counts for cryptococcal antigen before ART and for pre-emptive fluconazole in those who test positive. It covers evaluating antigen-positive people for meningitis and when to stop primary fluconazole prophylaxis, citing trials.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "source": "sections/sec-013-223-recommendations-for-children.md",
      "source_hash": "04a0d1ca7c19e429c0c4dd6e70eda9797121b591fc9bc337db368959fc247564",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that the screening and prophylaxis recommendations are not extended to children because the disease is rare in them, and introduces the new 2022 induction recommendation.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "source": "sections/sec-014-31-background.md",
      "source_hash": "1b900ee76321d909ce9043569316ca8dbf63383123470d817951d928cdd9a38f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the 2018 induction regimens for cryptococcal meningitis based on amphotericin B and flucytosine, along with alternatives when drugs are unavailable, and the extrapolation of evidence to children. It notes that fluconazole monotherapy is not recommended and that WHO met in 2022 to consider a single high-dose liposomal amphotericin B regimen.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "source": "sections/sec-015-3-recommendations-on-induction-consolidation-and.md",
      "source_hash": "ca8656127aaf8f3f53f85efe50886dcfe9df6acc7e66cd9f8e9f867fef2127d0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A section heading for the recommendations on induction, consolidation and maintenance antifungal treatment regimens.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "source": "sections/sec-016-32-induction-therapy.md",
      "source_hash": "337f832092e8b0995f9288bdb18035bec06def1fd5f1cdaceb6c42edd6762ef5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the 2022 recommendation of a single high dose of liposomal amphotericin B with 14 days of flucytosine and fluconazole as preferred induction therapy for cryptococcal meningitis. It lists alternative regimens for when liposomal amphotericin B, any amphotericin or flucytosine is unavailable and stresses the value of flucytosine.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "source": "sections/sec-017-321-rationale-for-the-recommendations.md",
      "source_hash": "f54d9b766568912ed24d739a3ecab79b03579e874b250c650f8f641f7bba6d41",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reviews the randomized trial in five African countries that compared single high-dose liposomal amphotericin B with the 2018 standard regimen in 844 people with cryptococcal meningitis. It reports that 10-week mortality was 24.8% versus 28.7%, showing non-inferiority, with fewer serious adverse events such as anaemia and kidney toxicity. The section also weighs costs, feasibility, acceptability and equity, noting the reduced burden on health workers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-018",
      "source": "sections/sec-018-33-preventing-monitoring-and-managing-amphoteric.md",
      "source_hash": "2e8140f175cff6f8589f717a1f6b46a685e19fc7374c7653871bf0dace20aa42",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out good practice principles for preventing, monitoring and managing amphotericin B toxicity, such as hypokalaemia, nephrotoxicity and anaemia. It describes pre-hydration, electrolyte supplementation and laboratory monitoring, and how to weigh continuing deoxycholate treatment when severe anaemia develops.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-019",
      "source": "sections/sec-019-34-drug-interactions.md",
      "source_hash": "c8055251063ca14218ce9183012b3e6bec5a4e2f7c6bb286c9ce361f30dbe359",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes possible interactions between antifungal drugs and ART, advising kidney monitoring and dose adjustment of tenofovir with amphotericin and haematological monitoring with flucytosine.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-020",
      "source": "sections/sec-020-35-consolidation-and-maintenance-treatment.md",
      "source_hash": "4fa75b55b14f372bce80b7cca39d2b5ea3c4e10a4c9c392c60aee6acf1702e8b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Restates the unchanged 2018 recommendations for fluconazole doses in the consolidation phase and in maintenance therapy until immune reconstitution.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-021",
      "source": "sections/sec-021-351-rationale-for-the-recommendations.md",
      "source_hash": "f090a468eda4ca0be009821da90b993e862482060e9cb4c13efec5c9e80b8a4a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains the evidence behind fluconazole consolidation and maintenance doses and its role in preventing relapse. It also suggests expert-opinion regimens for localized non-meningeal disease, cryptococcomas and disseminated disease.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-022",
      "source": "sections/sec-022-37-treatment-for-pregnant-women.md",
      "source_hash": "529b99f3c7c0ff8660158e11d6bad55c31d246ad431eb13049436e3e58c34740",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises that amphotericin B may be given in pregnancy when benefits outweigh harm, while flucytosine and fluconazole use should be judged case by case because of possible birth defects.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-023",
      "source": "sections/sec-023-38-adjunctive-corticosteroids-in-treating-hiv-as.md",
      "source_hash": "b0fbcf102e3c631be73b3ddcbbf40f4b794251e4e060693cf87b50e32c34a4e9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Restates the 2018 recommendation against routine adjunctive corticosteroids during induction treatment of cryptococcal meningitis, citing trial evidence of more disability and adverse events. It notes that a paediatric advisory group found no reason for a different approach in children.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-024",
      "source": "sections/sec-024-39-timing-of-art-initiation.md",
      "source_hash": "8131cdad060cc8ecc24aeadc8a1645d3358af6e5daa64733274d8ff660c67ff4",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Restates the 2018 recommendation that ART be deferred 4–6 weeks after starting antifungal treatment for cryptococcal meningitis because immediate ART raises mortality.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-025",
      "source": "sections/sec-025-391-rationale-for-the-recommendation.md",
      "source_hash": "032843fb9a388e8ccbc6ffbb0a7c41ddb67a2ced3249de727d6fca90db62508d",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains the evidence from four trials that early ART after cryptococcal meningitis increases mortality and specifies deferral periods depending on the induction regimen. It also discusses the limited evidence on ART timing for people who are antigen-positive without meningitis.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-026",
      "source": "sections/sec-026-392-implementation-considerations.md",
      "source_hash": "6b002acdb0785d16f787a2d576216171d5742ceb9a74b29f8df38e72e4565b95",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises evaluating people already on ART who develop cryptococcal meningitis for treatment failure and deferring any ART switch by four to six weeks.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-028",
      "source": "sections/sec-028-3101-raised-intracranial-pressure.md",
      "source_hash": "cebcd8630a2dd123d3993d3dffe6ec7938539d2e00e5854852ff038acdfdfed0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that raised intracranial pressure affects up to 80% of people with HIV-associated cryptococcal meningitis and that lowering it improves survival. It recommends an initial and early repeat lumbar puncture with pressure measurement regardless of symptoms, with therapeutic drainage when pressure is high. Practical notes cover settings without manometers and the volume of fluid that can be removed.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-029",
      "source": "sections/sec-029-3102-cryptococcal-immune-reconstitution-inflamma.md",
      "source_hash": "dcddcba4665b3fd624352ad5220fec6fa7677babdb94863240242d921458b871",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes cryptococcal immune reconstitution inflammatory syndrome after starting ART and lists management steps: continue ART, control intracranial pressure, optimize antifungals and consider short-course steroids for life-threatening deterioration.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
