    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-037",
      "source": "sections/sec-037-abstract.md",
      "source_hash": "1c28c30757dda71904dc2308956c413535689429d37126092c9151d55028af28",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The abstract of a systematic review on induction therapy for HIV-associated cryptococcal meningitis, which found one trial of 844 people comparing a single high dose of liposomal amphotericin B plus flucytosine and fluconazole with seven days of amphotericin deoxycholate. It reports that the single-dose regimen was non-inferior for 10-week mortality and caused fewer severe adverse events.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-038",
      "source": "sections/sec-038-background.md",
      "source_hash": "29531d7180ba3b01d19d289419b35e7e1939339d456168d753d1b42a1ce7d962",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Gives the background to the review, noting that cryptococcal meningitis is a leading cause of HIV deaths and that even the 2018 WHO-recommended regimen leaves high mortality and toxicity. It cites a trial in five African countries showing a single high dose of liposomal amphotericin B with two oral antifungals to be as effective, which prompted this update.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-039",
      "source": "sections/sec-039-methods.md",
      "source_hash": "2483fca580dea404c540de40aa265117439d0f82b36fbbe2e795b8f646f08d7c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the review methods, including eligibility of randomized trials comparing new induction regimens with WHO-recommended ones in people with a first episode of HIV-associated cryptococcal meningitis. It lists outcomes such as 2- and 10-week mortality, fungal clearance and serious laboratory adverse events, and explains the statistical analysis and use of GRADE for certainty.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-040",
      "source": "sections/sec-040-results.md",
      "source_hash": "d7305ad63c839f3d49d290e6c95a39ba66e740667e74edb8875a8012d796a0b9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports the study selection, in which one trial of 844 adults in Botswana, Malawi, South Africa, Uganda and Zimbabwe met the criteria, and describes its non-inferiority design. It summarizes the risk of bias and GRADE assessments, rating certainty low for mortality and fungal clearance and moderate for severe adverse events.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-357088/blocks/prose-sec-041",
      "source": "sections/sec-041-discussion.md",
      "source_hash": "b2c217ca7082e889d1b3be44c798418553d69a9e8c041f252b40181507cedf60",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses the findings, concluding that single high-dose liposomal amphotericin B with flucytosine and fluconazole was non-inferior to standard induction therapy with fewer adverse events. It notes the limitation of relying on one trial and differences between trial and routine settings, and states that WHO issued updated guidelines in March 2022 recommending the regimen, calling for wider access to the drugs.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
